<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Implementation Details</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We demonstrate results of MIRA on multiple reward functions, including Aesthetic Score, HPSv2, PickScore, and image brightness and darkness. The first three are human-aligned, whereas the last two are useful for easily visualizing reward hacking. We set <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=0.2</annotation></semantics></math> for Aesthetic Score, <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=0.5</annotation></semantics></math> for HPSv2 and PickScore, <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=1</annotation></semantics></math> for brightness, and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=0.8</annotation></semantics></math> for darkness. For JPEG compressibility, a non-differentiable reward, we use <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=1</annotation></semantics></math>. HPSv2 and PickScore use ViT-H/14 as the backbone, and Aesthetic Score uses ViT-L/14.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We implement MIRA with a learning rate of <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.01</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.01</annotation></semantics></math> and the AdamW optimizer in all experiments. Our method runs on a single A100 Nvidia GPU. For DNO, we use noise regularization (i.e. PRNO) unless otherwise stated. Other baselines use their default configurations.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">User Study Details.</span> We obtain these results from anonymous volunteers who respond using an online form. We ask these participants: <span id="A1.SS1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">“Which of the below images would you personally prefer getting given the above prompt (based on your personal trade-off between prompt faithfulness and aesthetics)?”</span> We adopt this from ReNO. Given side-by-side images (prompt-matched, order-randomized), participants have the option to choose the left image, the right image, or neither/both. In the case of the last option, we assign a score of <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5</annotation></semantics></math> to that image pair. Due to computational restrictions, we limit the number of participants to 100. We further limit the number of images to 50 to respect the participants’ time.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Algorithms</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the reader’s reference, we provide our loss for non-differentiable rewards as follows. Given prompt <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{MIRA-DPO}}=-\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}^{w},x_{0}^{l}}\log\!\sigma\Bigg(\!\beta\mathbb{E}_{\begin{subarray}{c}x_{1:T}^{w}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|x_{0}^{w},z^{w},c)\\
x_{1:T}^{l}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|x_{0}^{l},z^{l},c)\end{subarray}}\Bigg[\log\frac{p_{\theta}(x_{0:T}^{w}|z^{w},c)}{p_{\theta}(x_{0:T}^{w}|z_{0}^{w},c)}-\log\frac{p_{\theta}(x_{0:T}^{l}|z^{l},c)}{p_{\theta}(x_{0:T}^{l}|z_{0}^{l},c)}\Bigg]\!\Bigg)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>MIRA-DPO</mtext></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>w</mi></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>w</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>w</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>w</mi></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>w</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>w</mi></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>w</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mpadded style="width:0.108em;" width="0.108em"><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{MIRA-DPO}}=-\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}^{w},x_{0}^{l}}\log\!\sigma\Bigg(\!\beta\mathbb{E}_{\begin{subarray}{c}x_{1:T}^{w}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|x_{0}^{w},z^{w},c)\\
x_{1:T}^{l}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|x_{0}^{l},z^{l},c)\end{subarray}}\Bigg[\log\frac{p_{\theta}(x_{0:T}^{w}|z^{w},c)}{p_{\theta}(x_{0:T}^{w}|z_{0}^{w},c)}-\log\frac{p_{\theta}(x_{0:T}^{l}|z^{l},c)}{p_{\theta}(x_{0:T}^{l}|z_{0}^{l},c)}\Bigg]\!\Bigg).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> MIRA for Non-differentiable Rewards</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algx1.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
              
              
             Initial noise <math id="algx1.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{0}^{(1)},z_{0}^{(2)}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{0}^{(1)},z_{0}^{(2)}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math>, prompt <math id="algx1.l0.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>, reward function <math id="algx1.l0.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, sampling process <math id="algx1.l0.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, optimization steps <math id="algx1.l0.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\text{opt}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mtext>opt</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\text{opt}}</annotation></semantics></math>, learning rate <math id="algx1.l0.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, regularization hyperparameter <math id="algx1.l0.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
              
             Initialize <math id="algx1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{(1)}\leftarrow z_{0}^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{(1)}\leftarrow z_{0}^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="algx1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{(2)}\leftarrow z_{0}^{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{(2)}\leftarrow z_{0}^{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
              
             <span id="algx1.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="algx1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1,\dots,K_{\text{opt}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mtext>opt</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1,\dots,K_{\text{opt}}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx1.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="algx1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
              
              <math id="algx1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}^{(1)}\leftarrow G_{\theta}(z^{(1)},c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}^{(1)}\leftarrow G_{\theta}(z^{(1)},c)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx1.l3.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><span id="algx1.l3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">// Generate images</span>
</span>
</div>
<div id="algx1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
              
              
