<section id="A1.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.7 </span>GPT-4o Evaluation</h3>

<div id="A1.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We compute the win rate of generated images from our method and baselines, employing GPT-4o as the judge. In all experiments, we use a temperature of 0 and Top-p of 1. The instruction prompt is as follows, where “PROMPT” and “TARGET REWARD” are placeholders.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS7.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.SS7.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="495.87" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 600 495.87" width="600"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,495.87) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 489.96 C 0 493.22 2.64 495.87 5.91 495.87 L 594.09 495.87 C 597.36 495.87 600 493.22 600 489.96 L 600 5.91 C 600 2.64 597.36 0 594.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 471.91 L 598.03 471.91 L 598.03 5.91 C 598.03 3.73 596.27 1.97 594.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 480.51)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:40.23em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.15" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="556.67"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS7.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:40.23em;">
<span id="A1.SS7.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS7.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">System Prompt</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 13.78)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:40.23em;--ltx-fo-height:32.26em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="446.33" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 446.33)" width="556.67"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS7.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:40.23em;">
<span id="A1.SS7.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS7.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You are a helpful, impartial, and precise assistant tasked with evaluating two images based on a given text prompt, a reward criterion, and specific quality guidelines. The text prompt is: generate an image of a “PROMPT”. The reward criterion is: “TARGET REWARD.” Please compare the two images and evaluate them based on the following:</span></span>
<span id="A1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<span id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<span id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Adherence to the text prompt: Assess which image better satisfies the intent of the text prompt by being meaningful and directly relevant to the described subject. Do not use the reward criterion to determine adherence to the prompt.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<span id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Satisfaction of the reward criterion: Determine which image more effectively meets the reward criterion.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS7.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS7.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Choose the image that maximizes the reward without compromising adherence to the prompt.
With a lower priority, also ensure that:</span></span>
<span id="A1.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<span id="A1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<span id="A1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The image does not have overly vibrant colors or extreme sharpening.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;padding-top:0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<span id="A1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The lighting is balanced and natural.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A1.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;padding-top:0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<span id="A1.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The lighting is softer and more diffused.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A1.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;padding-top:0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<span id="A1.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A1.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The image appears realistic and natural, avoiding being overly saturated, sharpened, or monochromatic.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A1.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;padding-top:0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<span id="A1.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A1.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Shapes and objects are not overly simplified, distorted, or stylized.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A1.I2.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;padding-top:0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">6.</span> 
<span id="A1.I2.i6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A1.I2.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The image is not completely white or black, unless explicitly required.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A1.I2.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;padding-top:0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">7.</span> 
<span id="A1.I2.i7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A1.I2.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Relevant textures are present, and the image is not overly simplistic or missing essential details.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A1.I2.i8" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;padding-top:0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">8.</span> 
<span id="A1.I2.i8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A1.I2.i8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The composition is dynamic, creating a sense of energy and movement.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS7.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS7.p2.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">In the end, only output 1 if the first image is selected, or else output 2, and nothing else.</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS7.p2.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS7.p2.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">USER PROMPT<span id="A1.SS7.p2.pic1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS8" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.8 </span>Proof of Proposition 1</h3>

<div id="A1.SS8.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">To make our point that the change in the image distribution is unbounded with respect to the change in initial noise, we consider a simple setting with <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z:=x_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z:=x_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{T},\ldots,\epsilon_{1}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2}\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{T},\ldots,\epsilon_{1}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2}\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math>, and the following random process</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\theta x_{t}+\epsilon_{t}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\theta x_{t}+\epsilon_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS8.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS8.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">which holds from <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=T</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>. Now, applying the recursive relation starting from <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{T}=z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{T}=z</annotation></semantics></math>, we can write</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{T-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{T-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\theta z+\epsilon_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\theta z+\epsilon_{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{T-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{T-2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\theta x_{T-1}+\epsilon_{T-1}=\theta^{2}x_{T}+\theta\epsilon_{T}+\epsilon_{T-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\theta x_{T-1}+\epsilon_{T-1}=\theta^{2}x_{T}+\theta\epsilon_{T}+\epsilon_{T-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center" colspan="2"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\theta^{T}z+\sum_{k=1}^{T}\theta^{k-1}\epsilon_{T-k+1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\theta^{T}z+\sum_{k=1}^{T}\theta^{k-1}\epsilon_{T-k+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS8.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS8.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">This implies that the mean of <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is</span></p>
<table id="A1.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[x_{0}|z\right]=\theta^{T}z," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[x_{0}|z\right]=\theta^{T}z,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS8.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS8.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">and variance of <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> can be written as</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Var}(x_{0}|z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Var}(x_{0}|z)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Var}\!\left(\sum_{k=1}^{T}\theta^{k-1}\epsilon_{T-k+1}\right)=\sum_{k=1}^{T}\theta^{2k-2}\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.643em;" width="1.643em"><mtext>Var</mtext></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Var}\!\left(\sum_{k=1}^{T}\theta^{k-1}\epsilon_{T-k+1}\right)=\sum_{k=1}^{T}\theta^{2k-2}\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma^{2}\frac{\theta^{2T}-1}{\theta^{2}-1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma^{2}\frac{\theta^{2T}-1}{\theta^{2}-1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS8.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS8.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">and for simplicity we assume <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\theta\right|&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\theta\right|&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. From <a href="#A1.E10" title="In Proof. ‣ A.8 Proof of Proposition 1 ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ MIRA: Towards Mitigating Reward Hacking in Inference-Time Alignment of T2I Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eqs.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> and <a href="#A1.Ex5" title="In Proof. ‣ A.8 Proof of Proposition 1 ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ MIRA: Towards Mitigating Reward Hacking in Inference-Time Alignment of T2I Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>, we note that <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}\sim\mathcal{N}\bigg(\theta^{T}z,\sigma^{2}\frac{\theta^{2T}-1}{\theta^{2}-1}\bigg)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}\sim\mathcal{N}\bigg(\theta^{T}z,\sigma^{2}\frac{\theta^{2T}-1}{\theta^{2}-1}\bigg)</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose that we have two noises <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1},z_{2}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1},z_{2}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, for two close noise <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can write</span></p>
<table id="A1.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="d_{\text{KL}}\left[p(\cdot|z_{1})\|p(\cdot|z_{2})\right]=\frac{\theta^{2T}{(\theta^{2}-1)}}{2\sigma^{2}(\theta^{2T}-1)}\cdot(z_{1}-z_{2})^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{KL}}\left[p(\cdot|z_{1})\|p(\cdot|z_{2})\right]=\frac{\theta^{2T}{(\theta^{2}-1)}}{2\sigma^{2}(\theta^{2T}-1)}\cdot(z_{1}-z_{2})^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS8.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS8.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text">which holds from the closed-form expression of KL divergence between two Gaussian distributions. From the above expression in <a href="#A1.E12" title="In Proof. ‣ A.8 Proof of Proposition 1 ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ MIRA: Towards Mitigating Reward Hacking in Inference-Time Alignment of T2I Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>, we note that the rate of change is controlled by the term <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\theta^{2T}{(\theta^{2}-1)}}{2\sigma^{2}(\theta^{2T}-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\theta^{2T}{(\theta^{2}-1)}}{2\sigma^{2}(\theta^{2T}-1)}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is controlled by the norm of neural network parameter <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> which can be arbitrarily large in practice.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS8.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS8.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS8.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS9" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.9 </span>Derivation of the Practical Objective for Differentiable Rewards</h3>

<div id="A1.SS9.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here, we derive the score function approximation of our Lagrangian objective,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathcal{J}_{\text{MIRA}}(z,c)=\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}\big[r(x_{0},c)\big]-\beta d_{\text{KL}}\big[p_{\theta}(x_{0}|z,c)\ \|\ p_{\theta}(x_{0}|z_{0},c)\big].\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>MIRA</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>d</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo rspace="0.722em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="1.167em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathcal{J}_{\text{MIRA}}(z,c)=\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}\big[r(x_{0},c)\big]-\beta d_{\text{KL}}\big[p_{\theta}(x_{0}|z,c)\ \|\ p_{\theta}(x_{0}|z_{0},c)\big].\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS9.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS9.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We consider the <math id="A1.SS9.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{KL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{KL}}</annotation></semantics></math> term in <a href="#A1.E13" title="In A.9 Derivation of the Practical Objective for Differentiable Rewards ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ MIRA: Towards Mitigating Reward Hacking in Inference-Time Alignment of T2I Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a></p>
<table id="A1.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathcal{W}=d_{\text{KL}}\big[p_{\theta}(x_{0}|z,c)\ \|\ p_{\theta}(x_{0}|z_{0},c)\big].\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo rspace="0.722em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="1.167em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathcal{W}=d_{\text{KL}}\big[p_{\theta}(x_{0}|z,c)\ \|\ p_{\theta}(x_{0}|z_{0},c)\big].\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS9.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS9.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We need to show that we can minimize <math id="A1.SS9.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}</annotation></semantics></math> by minimizing</p>
<table id="A1.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathcal{W}^{\prime}\approx\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}\bigg[\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\sigma_{t}^{2}\left(\|s(x_{t}|z_{0},c)\|^{2}-\|s(x_{t}|z,c)\|^{2}\right)\bigg],\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≈</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathcal{W}^{\prime}\approx\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}\bigg[\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\sigma_{t}^{2}\left(\|s(x_{t}|z_{0},c)\|^{2}-\|s(x_{t}|z,c)\|^{2}\right)\bigg],\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS9.p3.2" class="ltx_p">with expectation over reverse trajectories <math id="A1.SS9.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS9.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS9.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS9.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS9.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">We start with <a href="#A1.E14" title="In A.9 Derivation of the Practical Objective for Differentiable Rewards ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ MIRA: Towards Mitigating Reward Hacking in Inference-Time Alignment of T2I Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a> and write it as follows:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathcal{W}=\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}\bigg[\log\frac{p_{\theta}(x_{0}|z,c)}{p_{\theta}(x_{0}|z_{0},c)}\bigg].\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathcal{W}=\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}\bigg[\log\frac{p_{\theta}(x_{0}|z,c)}{p_{\theta}(x_{0}|z_{0},c)}\bigg].\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS9.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS9.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS9.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that <math id="A1.SS9.p5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="d_{\text{KL}}\big[p_{\theta}(x_{0}|z,c)\|p_{\theta}(x_{0}|z_{0},c)\big]\leq d_{\text{KL}}\big[p_{\theta}(\tau|z,c)\|p_{\theta}(\tau|z_{0},c)\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{KL}}\big[p_{\theta}(x_{0}|z,c)\|p_{\theta}(x_{0}|z_{0},c)\big]\leq d_{\text{KL}}\big[p_{\theta}(\tau|z,c)\|p_{\theta}(\tau|z_{0},c)\big]</annotation></semantics></math>, establishing an upper bound. Therefore,</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS9.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{W}\leq\mathcal{W}^{\prime}=\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}\big[\log p_{\theta}(\tau|z,c)-\log p_{\theta}(\tau|z_{0},c)\big]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{W}\leq\mathcal{W}^{\prime}=\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}\big[\log p_{\theta}(\tau|z,c)-\log p_{\theta}(\tau|z_{0},c)\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS9.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS9.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS9.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">By linearity of expectation, this is</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{W^{\prime}}=\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}\big[\log p_{\theta}(\tau|z,c)\big]-\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}\big[\log p_{\theta}(\tau|z_{0},c)\big]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{W^{\prime}}=\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}\big[\log p_{\theta}(\tau|z,c)\big]-\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}\big[\log p_{\theta}(\tau|z_{0},c)\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS9.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS9.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS9.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let us focus on the term <math id="A1.SS9.p8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}[\log p_{\theta}(\tau|z,c)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}[\log p_{\theta}(\tau|z,c)]</annotation></semantics></math>, which we can expand as</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}[\log p_{\theta}(\tau|z,c)]=\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}\left[\log\prod_{t=0}^{T-1}p_{\theta}(x_{t}|x_{t+1},z,c)\right].\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>]</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}[\log p_{\theta}(\tau|z,c)]=\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}\left[\log\prod_{t=0}^{T-1}p_{\theta}(x_{t}|x_{t+1},z,c)\right].\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS9.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS9.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS9.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">We can expand <a href="#A1.E19" title="In Proof. ‣ A.9 Derivation of the Practical Objective for Differentiable Rewards ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ MIRA: Towards Mitigating Reward Hacking in Inference-Time Alignment of T2I Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a> as</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS9.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}[\log p_{\theta}(\tau|z,c)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}[\log p_{\theta}(\tau|z,c)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 42.67912pt=\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}\Bigg[\log\left(\exp\bigg(-\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\frac{\|x_{t}-\mu_{\theta}(x_{t+1},z,c)\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\bigg)\prod_{t=0}^{T-1}\frac{1}{\sigma_{t}\sqrt{2\pi}}\right)\Bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 42.67912pt=\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}\Bigg[\log\left(\exp\bigg(-\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\frac{\|x_{t}-\mu_{\theta}(x_{t+1},z,c)\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\bigg)\prod_{t=0}^{T-1}\frac{1}{\sigma_{t}\sqrt{2\pi}}\right)\Bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 42.67912pt=\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}\Bigg[-\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\frac{\|x_{t}-\mu_{\theta}(x_{t+1},z,c)\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\Bigg]+\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\log\frac{1}{\sigma_{t}\sqrt{2\pi}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 42.67912pt=\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}\Bigg[-\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\frac{\|x_{t}-\mu_{\theta}(x_{t+1},z,c)\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\Bigg]+\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\log\frac{1}{\sigma_{t}\sqrt{2\pi}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS9.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS9.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS9.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS9.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\theta}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\theta}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is the predicted mean of the Gaussian at each step of the reverse process. We also know that for a Gaussian distribution,</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS9.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\|s(x_{t}|z,c)\|=\|\nabla_{x_{t}}\log p(x_{t}|z,c)\|\approx\|\nabla_{x_{t}}\log p_{\theta}(x_{t}|x_{t+1};z,c)\|,\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\|s(x_{t}|z,c)\|=\|\nabla_{x_{t}}\log p(x_{t}|z,c)\|\approx\|\nabla_{x_{t}}\log p_{\theta}(x_{t}|x_{t+1};z,c)\|,\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A1.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\|s(x_{t}|z,c)\|\approx\left\|\nabla_{x_{t}}\log\left(\frac{1}{\sigma_{t}\sqrt{2\pi}}\exp\left(-\frac{\|x_{t}-\mu_{\theta}(x_{t+1},t+1,z,c)\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\right)\right)\right\|,\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\|s(x_{t}|z,c)\|\approx\left\|\nabla_{x_{t}}\log\left(\frac{1}{\sigma_{t}\sqrt{2\pi}}\exp\left(-\frac{\|x_{t}-\mu_{\theta}(x_{t+1},t+1,z,c)\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\right)\right)\right\|,\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A1.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\|s(x_{t}|z,c)\|\approx\left\|-\frac{x_{t}-\mu_{\theta}(x_{t+1},t+1,z,c)}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}\right\|.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\|s(x_{t}|z,c)\|\approx\left\|-\frac{x_{t}-\mu_{\theta}(x_{t+1},t+1,z,c)}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}\right\|.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS9.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS9.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS9.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Replacing <a href="#A1.E23" title="In Proof. ‣ A.9 Derivation of the Practical Objective for Differentiable Rewards ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ MIRA: Towards Mitigating Reward Hacking in Inference-Time Alignment of T2I Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a> in <a href="#A1.Ex6" title="In Proof. ‣ A.9 Derivation of the Practical Objective for Differentiable Rewards ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ MIRA: Towards Mitigating Reward Hacking in Inference-Time Alignment of T2I Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>, we get</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}[\log p_{\theta}(\tau|z,c)]\approx\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}\Bigg[-\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\|s(x_{t}|z,c)\|^{2}\frac{\sigma_{t}^{2}}{2}\Bigg]+\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\log\frac{1}{\sigma_{t}\sqrt{2\pi}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≈</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}[\log p_{\theta}(\tau|z,c)]\approx\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}\Bigg[-\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\|s(x_{t}|z,c)\|^{2}\frac{\sigma_{t}^{2}}{2}\Bigg]+\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\log\frac{1}{\sigma_{t}\sqrt{2\pi}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS9.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS9.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS9.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Applying <a href="#A1.E24" title="In Proof. ‣ A.9 Derivation of the Practical Objective for Differentiable Rewards ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ MIRA: Towards Mitigating Reward Hacking in Inference-Time Alignment of T2I Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a> to <a href="#A1.E17" title="In Proof. ‣ A.9 Derivation of the Practical Objective for Differentiable Rewards ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ MIRA: Towards Mitigating Reward Hacking in Inference-Time Alignment of T2I Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>, we get</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{W^{\prime}}\approx\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}\left[\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\left(\|s(x_{t}|z_{0},c)\|^{2}-\|s(x_{t}|z,c)\|^{2}\right)\sigma_{t}^{2}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≈</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{W^{\prime}}\approx\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}\left[\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\left(\|s(x_{t}|z_{0},c)\|^{2}-\|s(x_{t}|z,c)\|^{2}\right)\sigma_{t}^{2}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS9.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS9.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS9.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">We can use <a href="#A1.E25" title="In Proof. ‣ A.9 Derivation of the Practical Objective for Differentiable Rewards ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ MIRA: Towards Mitigating Reward Hacking in Inference-Time Alignment of T2I Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a> in <a href="#A1.E13" title="In A.9 Derivation of the Practical Objective for Differentiable Rewards ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ MIRA: Towards Mitigating Reward Hacking in Inference-Time Alignment of T2I Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>. Our final objective is</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathcal{J}_{\text{MIRA}}(z,c)\!=\!\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}\big[r(x_{0},c)\big]-\beta\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}\bigg[\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\sigma_{t}^{2}\left(\|s(x_{t}|z_{0},c)\|^{2}-\|s(x_{t}|z,c)\|^{2}\right)\bigg].\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>MIRA</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mpadded style="width:0.327em;" width="0.327em"><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mpadded><mpadded style="width:0.716em;" width="0.716em"><mo>=</mo></mpadded><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathcal{J}_{\text{MIRA}}(z,c)\!=\!\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}\big[r(x_{0},c)\big]-\beta\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}\bigg[\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\sigma_{t}^{2}\left(\|s(x_{t}|z_{0},c)\|^{2}-\|s(x_{t}|z,c)\|^{2}\right)\bigg].\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS9.p15.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS9.p15.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS10" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.10 </span>Derivation of DPO Objective</h3>

<div id="A1.SS10.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We begin with our original objective,</p>
<table id="A1.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\max_{z}\mathcal{J}_{\text{MIRA}}(z,c)=\max_{z}\left[\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}\big[r(x_{0},c)\big]-\beta d_{\text{KL}}\left[p_{\theta}(x_{0}|z,c)\ \!\|\!\ p_{\theta}(x_{0}|z_{0},c)\right]\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>z</mi></munder><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>MIRA</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>z</mi></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo rspace="0.052em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{z}\mathcal{J}_{\text{MIRA}}(z,c)=\max_{z}\left[\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}\big[r(x_{0},c)\big]-\beta d_{\text{KL}}\left[p_{\theta}(x_{0}|z,c)\ \!\|\!\ p_{\theta}(x_{0}|z_{0},c)\right]\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS10.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS10.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS10.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R(x_{0:T},c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(x_{0:T},c)</annotation></semantics></math> be the reward along the whole sampling trajectory such that</p>
<table id="A1.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="r(x_{0},c):=\mathbb{E}_{x_{1:T}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|x_{0},z,c)}\left[R(x_{0:T},c)\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(x_{0},c):=\mathbb{E}_{x_{1:T}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|x_{0},z,c)}\left[R(x_{0:T},c)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS10.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS10.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This means</p>
<table id="A1.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{z}\mathcal{J}_{\text{MIRA}}(z,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>z</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>MIRA</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{z}\mathcal{J}_{\text{MIRA}}(z,c)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex8.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\max_{z}\left[\mathbb{E}_{\begin{subarray}{c}x_{0}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)\\
x_{1:T}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|x_{0},z,c)\end{subarray}}\left[R(x_{0:T},c)\right]-\beta d_{\text{KL}}\left[p_{\theta}(x_{0}|z,c)\ \!\|\!\ p_{\theta}(x_{0}|z_{0},c)\right]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>z</mi></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo rspace="0.052em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\max_{z}\left[\mathbb{E}_{\begin{subarray}{c}x_{0}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)\\
x_{1:T}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|x_{0},z,c)\end{subarray}}\left[R(x_{0:T},c)\right]-\beta d_{\text{KL}}\left[p_{\theta}(x_{0}|z,c)\ \!\|\!\ p_{\theta}(x_{0}|z_{0},c)\right]\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\min_{z}\left[-\mathbb{E}_{\begin{subarray}{c}x_{0}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)\\
x_{1:T}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|x_{0},z,c)\end{subarray}}\left[R(x_{0:T},c)\right]+\beta d_{\text{KL}}\left[p_{\theta}(x_{0}|z,c)\ \!\|\!\ p_{\theta}(x_{0}|z_{0},c)\right]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>z</mi></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo rspace="0.052em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\min_{z}\left[-\mathbb{E}_{\begin{subarray}{c}x_{0}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)\\
x_{1:T}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|x_{0},z,c)\end{subarray}}\left[R(x_{0:T},c)\right]+\beta d_{\text{KL}}\left[p_{\theta}(x_{0}|z,c)\ \!\|\!\ p_{\theta}(x_{0}|z_{0},c)\right]\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\min_{z}\left[-\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}\bigg[\mathbb{E}_{x_{1:T}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}\left[R(x_{0:T},c)\right]-\beta\log\frac{p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}{p_{\theta}(\cdot|z_{0},c)}\bigg]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>z</mi></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\min_{z}\left[-\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}\bigg[\mathbb{E}_{x_{1:T}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}\left[R(x_{0:T},c)\right]-\beta\log\frac{p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}{p_{\theta}(\cdot|z_{0},c)}\bigg]\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\min_{z}\left[\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}\bigg[\log\frac{p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}{p_{\theta}(\cdot|z_{0},c)}-\frac{1}{\beta}\mathbb{E}_{x_{1:T}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|x_{0},z,c)}\left[R(x_{0:T},c)\right]\bigg]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>z</mi></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\min_{z}\left[\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}\bigg[\log\frac{p_{\theta}(\cdot|z,c)}{p_{\theta}(\cdot|z_{0},c)}-\frac{1}{\beta}\mathbb{E}_{x_{1:T}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|x_{0},z,c)}\left[R(x_{0:T},c)\right]\bigg]\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
